{
  "_comment": [
    "Closed vocabularies for scripts/armor_names.py.",
    "slots: fr = French noun, g = grammatical gender (m/f), n = number (s/p).",
    "  Gender and number drive colour-adjective agreement, so they must be right.",
    "colours: the four agreement forms (ms/fs/mp/fp). Invariable adjectives",
    "  (azur, orange, rose, emeraude, jade) simply repeat the same form.",
    "tiers: upgrade-stage codes. HS = 狩護 (Chassegarde), GS/GP = G級狩護.",
    "  The codes are deliberately kept as-is: they are already Latin letters in",
    "  the Japanese source (ラヴィHSアーム), the English patch keeps them, and every",
    "  wiki including the Japanese ones uses them. « Chassegarde » translates the",
    "  word where it is spelled out (the ≪…≫ markers in equipment descriptions),",
    "  it does not recode these 18038 names. See glossary.fr.md §7.",
    "classes: weapon-class marker after the colon (EN patch uses BM/GN)."
  ],
